1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,143
Electrode potentials depend on concentration, temperature and gas pressure.

2
00:00:05,143 --> 00:00:12,812
So we fix standard conditions: two ninety eight kelvin, all ions at one molar, all gases at one bar.

3
00:00:12,812 --> 00:00:18,932
Measured against the hydrogen electrode, that gives the standard electrode potential, E nought.

